Below is a plain ASCII text list of the extended FreeRTOS OS interfaces. Note that this list is based on the general FreeRTOS distribution and may vary slightly with version or configuration.

------------------------------------------------------------
FREE_RTOS OS INTERFACES - EXTENDED LIST (ASCII FORMAT)
------------------------------------------------------------

1. TASK MANAGEMENT
   ----------------
   a. Task Creation and Deletion:
      - xTaskCreate()
      - xTaskCreateStatic()
      - vTaskDelete()

   b. Task Control & State Management:
      - vTaskDelay()
      - vTaskDelayUntil()
      - vTaskSuspend()
      - vTaskResume()
      - taskYIELD()    (voluntary yield)
      - vTaskPrioritySet()
      - uxTaskPriorityGet()
      - xTaskNotify(), xTaskNotifyGive(), ulTaskNotifyTake()
      - vTaskSuspendAll(), xTaskResumeAll()
      - uxTaskGetNumberOfTasks()
      - vTaskGetInfo()          (for task details)
      - vTaskGetRunTimeStats()  (for execution statistics)
      - Trace macros (e.g., traceTASK_SWITCHED_IN())

2. INTER-TASK COMMUNICATION
   --------------------------
   a. Queues:
      - xQueueCreate()
      - xQueueSend()
      - xQueueSendToBack()
      - xQueueSendToFront()
      - xQueueReceive()
      - xQueuePeek()
      (Plus additional queue management functions)

   b. Direct-to-Task Notifications:
      - (Integrated into task APIs as lightweight signaling)

   c. Message Buffers:
      - xMessageBufferCreate()
      - xMessageBufferSend()
      - xMessageBufferReceive()

   d. Stream Buffers:
      - xStreamBufferCreate()
      - xStreamBufferSend()
      - xStreamBufferReceive()

3. SYNCHRONIZATION MECHANISMS
   ----------------------------
   a. Semaphores:
      - xSemaphoreCreateBinary()
      - xSemaphoreTake()
      - xSemaphoreGive()
      - xSemaphoreCreateCounting()
      - ISR Variants: xSemaphoreGiveFromISR(), xSemaphoreTakeFromISR()

   b. Mutexes:
      - xSemaphoreCreateMutex()
      - xSemaphoreCreateRecursiveMutex()
      - xSemaphoreTakeRecursive()
      - xSemaphoreGiveRecursive()

   c. Event Groups:
      - xEventGroupCreate()
      - xEventGroupSetBits()
      - xEventGroupClearBits()
      - xEventGroupWaitBits()
      - (Includes ISR-safe variants)

4. TIME MANAGEMENT
   -----------------
   a. Software Timers:
      - xTimerCreate()
      - xTimerStart()
      - xTimerStop()
      - xTimerReset()
      - xTimerChangePeriod()
      (Timers run in their own timer task context)

   b. Hook Functions:
      - vApplicationTickHook()       (called at each RTOS tick)
      - vApplicationIdleHook()       (called when idle)
      - vApplicationMallocFailedHook() (called on allocation failure)

5. MEMORY MANAGEMENT
   -------------------
   a. Dynamic Memory Allocation Schemes:
      - heap_1 (simplest: allocation only, no free)
      - heap_2 (allows allocation and freeing, basic coalescing)
      - heap_3 (wraps standard C library malloc/free)
      - heap_4 (improved coalescence, reduced fragmentation)
      - heap_5 (supports multiple non-contiguous regions)

   b. Core Allocation APIs:
      - pvPortMalloc()
      - vPortFree()

6. INTERRUPT HANDLING & ISR-SAFE INTERFACES
   ------------------------------------------
   - xQueueSendFromISR()
   - xQueueReceiveFromISR()
   - xSemaphoreGiveFromISR()
   - xTaskNotifyFromISR()
   - (Other ISR-safe versions as needed)

7. PORTABILITY & HARDWARE ABSTRACTION
   ------------------------------------
   a. Port Layer:
      - Context Switching (assembly routines/intrinsic functions)
      - Critical Section Management (enter/exit critical sections)
      - System Tick Configuration (timer setup for RTOS tick)

   b. Architecture-Specific Utilities:
      - CPU/Compiler-specific macros and utilities found in the "portable" folder

8. OPTIONAL & DEBUG/TRACE UTILITIES
   ---------------------------------
   a. Run-Time Stats and Tracing:
      - vTaskGetRunTimeStats()  (for task execution times)
      - Trace macros/hooks for third-party tools integration

   b. Additional Utilities:
      - Internal list and queue utilities (for debugging/tuning)
      - configASSERT() macro (to catch programming/configuration errors)

------------------------------------------------------------
Note: This list is as complete as possible for the core and common optional interfaces in FreeRTOS. Specific versions or additional modules (e.g., TCP/IP stacks, file systems) may introduce more interfaces.
------------------------------------------------------------